# Cancel is a request, not an outcome. `stopped` is the only field that may be
# read as "the motion ended"; the contract keeps those two apart because the
# difference is what stops a new task being handed to a robot that is still
# moving. A cancel that cannot be confirmed leaves the payload and any resource
# held by the old task alone.

string task_id
---
bool accepted
bool stopped
string state
string reason_code
string message
